# Exercises every Payment endpoint against the compose stack (`docker compose up -d --build`).
# Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the token requests store tokens for
# the ones after them. Each change also publishes a payment.payment event; the README shows how to
# watch the topic.
# Its client and webhook secrets are the stack's own: run it in the `dev` environment, whose
# http-client.private.env.json holds them (the root README's "Secrets" says how to write it).

@payment = http://localhost:8084
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@userinfo = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/userinfo
@gateway = http://localhost:8000/api/payment

### Customer token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo&scope=openid

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The demo Customer's ID: the sub the checkout Saga names in the body
GET {{userinfo}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("customerId", response.body.sub); %}

### Orchestration token: the checkout Saga's own identity, for the commands it calls
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=orchestration&client_secret={{orchestrationClientSecret}}

> {% client.global.set("orchestrationToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### The checkout Saga authorizes an Order's payment for the Customer: 201, AUTHORIZED by the approving test card, with its AUTHORIZATION transaction
< {% client.global.set("authorizeKey", $random.uuid); %}
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{authorizeKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("paymentId", response.body.id); %}

### The same request with the same key: the first response again, Idempotent-Replayed: true, and nothing more is authorized
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{authorizeKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### Without a key: 400, idempotencyKeyRequired
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### The Customer reads it back with their own token
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The same, through the API gateway
GET {{gateway}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Customer's Payments for the Order, newest first, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/payments?orderId=order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Saga voids it: 200, VOIDED, with a VOID transaction
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Voiding it again: the same 200, and nothing more is recorded
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### The gateway hides the commands: 404
POST {{gateway}}/payments/{{paymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A declining test card: 201, recorded as DECLINED with its declineReason, card_declined
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-2", "paymentMethod": "tok_decline", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("declinedPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### The Customer reads the declined Payment back too
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{declinedPaymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A declined Payment can't be voided: 409, paymentNotVoidable
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{declinedPaymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Not enough funds: DECLINED, insufficient_funds
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-3", "paymentMethod": "tok_insufficient_funds", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### A token the mock doesn't know: DECLINED, unknown_payment_method
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-4", "paymentMethod": "tok_visa", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### The gateway fails to answer: 502, and no Payment is recorded
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-5", "paymentMethod": "tok_gateway_error", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### No paymentMethod: 400
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### An unknown Payment: 404
GET {{payment}}/payments/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### An amount that isn't positive: 400
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 0, "currency": "EUR"}}

### An unknown currency: 400
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "XYZ"}}

### A Customer can't authorize a payment, only Orchestration can: 403
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### Without a token: 401
POST {{payment}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Staff read every Payment for an Order, with its transactions, through the gateway
GET {{gateway}}/staff/payments?orderId=order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A Customer can't: 403
GET {{gateway}}/staff/payments?orderId=order-1
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Staff read Payments only under /staff/payments: 403
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{paymentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Orchestration authorizes an Order's payment under a key of the Saga's shape: 201, AUTHORIZED
< {% client.global.set("sagaAuthorizeKey", "http-file-" + $random.uuid + ":run-1:authorizePayment"); %}
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{sagaAuthorizeKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-saga-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("sagaPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### Orchestration reads the Order's Payments, naming the Customer, as the fulfillment Saga does to find the one to capture
GET {{payment}}/payments/by-order?orderId=order-saga-1&customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### Orchestration reads it, naming the Customer, as the Saga does while it awaits settlement
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}/for-customer?customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### Naming another Customer: 404
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}/for-customer?customerId=someone-else
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### Orchestration voids it: 200, VOIDED; voiding again is the same 200
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A Customer can't read as Orchestration does: 403
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}/for-customer?customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A Customer naming a customer still reads their own Payment: 200
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{sagaPaymentId}}?customerId=someone-else
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A card the bank confirms later: 201, PENDING, until the mock's webhook settles it ~3 seconds on
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-async-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_async_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {%
  client.global.set("asyncPaymentId", response.body.id);
  client.global.set("asyncReference", response.body.gatewayReference);
%}

### A few seconds later: AUTHORIZED, its second AUTHORIZATION carrying the webhook's event ID
GET {{payment}}/payments/{{asyncPaymentId}}/for-customer?customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}

### The gateway's webhook, signed as the mock signs it, with the stack's webhook secret, through the API
### gateway without a token: 200, and nothing changes, since the Payment is settled already
< {%
  const body = JSON.stringify({eventId: "evt-http-" + $random.uuid, reference: client.global.get("asyncReference"), outcome: "DECLINED", declineReason: "card_declined"});
  request.variables.set("webhookBody", body);
  request.variables.set("webhookSignature", "sha256=" + crypto.hmac.sha256().withTextSecret(request.environment.get("paymentWebhookSecret")).updateWithText(body).digest().toHex());
%}
POST {{gateway}}/webhooks/gateway
Gateway-Signature: {{webhookSignature}}
Content-Type: application/json

{{webhookBody}}

### A webhook with a wrong signature: 401
POST {{gateway}}/webhooks/gateway
Gateway-Signature: sha256=00
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": "evt-forged", "reference": "{{asyncReference}}", "outcome": "DECLINED", "declineReason": "card_declined"}

### Capture: authorize an Order's payment for the fulfillment Saga to capture
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-capture-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("capturePaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### Orchestration captures it: 200, CAPTURED, with an approved CAPTURE transaction for the full amount
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{capturePaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Capturing it again, with another key: the same 200, and nothing more is recorded
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{capturePaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A captured Payment can't be voided: 409, alreadyCaptured
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{capturePaymentId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Capturing without a key: 400, idempotencyKeyRequired
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{capturePaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A Customer can't capture, only Orchestration can: 403
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{capturePaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### The API gateway hides the capture: 404
POST {{gateway}}/payments/{{capturePaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### A declined Payment can't be captured: 409, paymentNotCapturable
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{declinedPaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### The test card whose capture is refused: 201, AUTHORIZED
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-capture-2", "paymentMethod": "tok_capture_decline", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("refusedPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### Capturing it: 402, captureDeclined, authorization_expired; it stays AUTHORIZED, with a declined CAPTURE transaction
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refusedPaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Staff see its transactions, the declined CAPTURE among them
GET {{gateway}}/staff/payments?orderId=order-capture-2
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Refund: authorize and capture an Order's payment for the returns Saga to refund
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-refund-1", "paymentMethod": "tok_approve", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("refundPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### Orchestration captures it: 200, CAPTURED
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Orchestration refunds part of it for an RMA: 200, PARTIALLY_REFUNDED, with an approved REFUND transaction naming the RMA
< {% client.global.set("refundKey", "http-file-" + $random.uuid + ":run-1:refundPayment"); %}
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{refundKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 30000, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-3F2A9C1B"}

### The same request with the same key: the first response again, Idempotent-Replayed: true, and nothing more is refunded
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{refundKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 30000, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-3F2A9C1B"}

### More than is left: 422, refundExceedsCaptured, and nothing is recorded
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 49901, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000AAAA"}

### The rest: 200, REFUNDED
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 49900, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000AAAA"}

### A refunded Payment can't be refunded again: 409, paymentNotRefundable
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 1, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000BBBB"}

### An authorized Payment that was never captured can't be refunded: 409, paymentNotRefundable
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refusedPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 100, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000CCCC"}

### A Customer can't refund, only Orchestration can: 403
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 100, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000DDDD"}

### The API gateway hides the Refund: 404
POST {{gateway}}/payments/{{refundPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 100, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000EEEE"}

### The test card whose Refunds are refused: 201, AUTHORIZED
POST {{payment}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "orderId": "order-refund-2", "paymentMethod": "tok_refund_decline", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}}

> {% client.global.set("refundRefusedPaymentId", response.body.id); %}

### Captured: 200, CAPTURED
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundRefusedPaymentId}}/capture
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}"}

### Refunding it: 402, refundDeclined, refund_window_closed; it stays CAPTURED, with a declined REFUND transaction
POST {{payment}}/payments/{{refundRefusedPaymentId}}/refunds
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": {"amountMinor": 79900, "currency": "EUR"}, "reference": "RMA-0000FFFF"}

### Staff see the refunded Payment's transactions, each REFUND with its reference
GET {{gateway}}/staff/payments?orderId=order-refund-1
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
